<Base title="About" description="Matt Culwell writes The Sovereign Journal from Ada, Oklahoma. Chickasaw citizen. Founder of Sovereign Shield Technologies.">
  <p class="kicker">The author</p>
  <h1 class="page-title">{config.author}</h1>
  <p class="lede">{config.authorLine}</p>
  <div class="rule"></div>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>I founded Sovereign Shield Technologies in Ada, on Chickasaw land, to build the sovereign hyperscaler for nations and communities. The work is a closed-loop node: Native-owned waste-to-energy, compute sized to what that energy actually produces, and software that keeps community data on the community's side of the wall.</p>
    <p>Adaptive Inclusive Leadership Theory is the framework underneath that architecture. I developed it through doctoral research in Strategic Leadership. The book and the practice tools live at the <a href="https://ailt-leadership.vercel.app">AILT Institute</a>. The theory itself stays with Sovereign Shield as Layer 1 of the stack. Governance before compute.</p>
    <p>This journal is the daily record. One idea. One concrete anchor. A cost named out loud. It is written in the same voice I use when a node is late, not the voice I use when a slide is on time.</p>
    <h2>Why the work exists</h2>
    <blockquote>The four people I do everything for are the four people I could not do one thing for.</blockquote>
    <p>My mother. Cancer caught too late. Sovereign Health OS exists because of that. My father. Lost when twenty-four hour home care became impossible alone. CareCircle exists because of that. My wife's father. Heart attack at fifty-three, found three days later. Wearable monitoring exists because of that. My wife's mother. Died around fifty-six.</p>
    <p>Three children. Empty chairs at grandparents day on both sides. We are building it for the next family, in sovereign and rural communities, not as a slogan for a coast.</p>
    <h2>How to read</h2>
    <p>Start with the <a href="/">latest entry</a>, or with the <a href="/theory/">six constructs</a>. The <a href="/stack/">stack</a> page is the architecture without a pitch. Subscribe by RSS if you still do that. Medium readers can import any entry by pasting its address.</p>
    <p>Company site: <a href="https://www.sovereignshieldtechnologies.com">sovereignshieldtechnologies.com</a>.</p>
